    <item>
      <title>The Mighty Sparrow, Trinidadian Titan of Calypso, Is Dead at 91</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/27/arts/music/the-mighty-sparrow-dead.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/27/arts/music/the-mighty-sparrow-dead.html</guid>
      <atom:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/27/arts/music/the-mighty-sparrow-dead.html" rel="standout"></atom:link>
      <description>He was sometimes described as the last of the true calypso singers. But in fact he simultaneously preserved calypso tradition and invented it anew.</description>
      <dc:creator>Margalit Fox</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:59:29 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Mighty Sparrow</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Deaths (Obituaries)</category>
      <category domain="">Calypso (Music)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Music</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">Trinidad and Tobago</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Belafonte, Harry</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Powell, Colin L</category>
      <media:content height="1801" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/09/27/multimedia/27sparrow-pblq/27sparrow-pblq-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:credit>David Gonzalez/The New York Times</media:credit>
      <media:description>The Mighty Sparrow in 2013. Known as the king of calypso, he was renowned for his sonorous voice, unremitting energy and the sly double-entendre that are among the hallmarks of calypso lyrics.</media:description>
    </item>
